row 1) can print choices that do not fit its question, which is misleading for a grade 3 learner. The same mismatch applies to the numeral members printed beside a phrase-answer row. (2) Vocabulary gate: the words horizontal, vertical, diagonal, isosceles, equilateral and scalene are not in cumulative_vocab or introduces_vocab for this lc, and NOT_YET_KNOWN is empty, so the packet does not show them as introduced here. They are printed by F03 {answer} (horizontal, vertical, a scalene triangle), F04 {member} (horizontal, diagonal, equilateral), F05 and F03 {answer} from _ITEM_POOL (horizontal, vertical, scalene), F06 {distractors} (horizontal, diagonal) and F07 {question} (equilateral, isosceles, scalene, plus the bank question text). Families F01 and F02 pass. Clause verdicts are unaffected by the gate failure; all four clauses are reached through F07 {question}.\"}",
